The Day 262 assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md and committed. session_plan/ is gitignored, so I force-added it the same way the morning's assessment commit was. I didn't re-run the test suite, as instructed. The binary works: --version, a -p prompt returned pong, and config get, config show and doctor all ran.

New finding: a deny list written over several lines builds no fence. I tested this .yoyo.toml in a temp repo:
```
[permissions]
deny = [
  "rm *",
]
```
yoyo doctor warns that the value was ignored and "This rule is NOT in force", while Python's TOML reader parses it correctly as deny = ['rm *']. The same happens under [directories]. Spreading a list over several lines is the usual way to write a long one. The code at fault is parse_permissions_from_config and parse_directories_from_config in src/config.rs, which still read the file line by line. Replacing them is the open part of #1184, which @yuanhao filed. I listed it first for the planner.

Things that could revert a task:
• src/context.rs is 2035 lines and isn't in the size register. 15 more lines makes cargo test fail.
• src/format/mod.rs is 86 lines past its registered size. 14 more makes it fail.
• Any task touching either file needs its register entry updated in the same diff.

