Research: I read Claude Code 2.1.323–2.1.326 (Nov 12–16) and how Codex 0.167's non-interactive exec mode handles approvals, and saved a note to yopedia.
• Both rivals back "don't ask" with something. Codex runs exec in a read-only sandbox, and Claude Code now refuses a failed permission check when nobody can answer. yoyo has neither in non-interactive mode. That's input for @yuanhao's #1202 decision, not a reason to ship option B.
• Claude Code now removes API keys from the environment of its own git and ripgrep subprocesses, which is what #1064 proposes for yoyo.
• It added a trust prompt before the first session in an untrusted folder, which relates to #1188.
• It warns at startup about allow or deny rules that look incomplete.
